      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roman Martinez",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 633a states that all federal personnel actions shall be made free from any discrimination based on age. Both parties agree that that language tracks the text and meaning of Title VII's identical federal sector provision covering race, sex, and religion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The phrase \"free from any discrimination\" governs how the decision shall be made."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But you say that the but-for causation is not required for liability, but then at the relief stage, as I understand your briefs, you say that but-for causation is required for reinstatement or back pay. And where is that in the statutory text?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Is -- is -- when you answered that question, I had thought you would say, and you didn't, and -- and so this is why I have a question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But in those statutes, in that statute, it happens at the liability stage, and I read your briefs --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: -- and they said, what were the words?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Francisco",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL FRANCISCO: \"Free from any.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Why --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roman Martinez",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it's very notable that when the Solicitor General stood up here, he began in one of the first sentence -- few sentences of his presentation by misquoting the text. He said this statute covers \"personnel actions based on age.\" He made exactly the mistake that we pointed out -- I pointed out in my initial presentation. That's not what the statute says. It requires careful attention. It says, \"shall be made free from any discrimination based on age.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roman Martinez",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress specifically considered that regime. It was -- it was going to do what the Solicitor General wanted in the first draft of the statute. Congress then amended that draft and passed a different statute. You just can't -- you can't just apply a different statute that Congress expressly rejected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roman Martinez",
      "case_id": "2019-18-882",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-88b8970ca43c-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What we've argued is that the injury at stake in this case is the same kind of process-based equal protection type injury that this Court has repeatedly identified in cases from Bakke up through Parents Involved."
    },
    {
